F214 — sizeof(Array<uint64, 8>) does not parse

    error: Expected r_paren but got comma (,) in sizeof expr

The sizeof operand was always parsed as an expression, which stops at the first comma. Every QPI
container takes at least two template arguments, so this is how a contract asks how big its own
state is; aliasing the type first already worked, which is what isolated it to the operand path
rather than the type parser.

When an IDENTIFIER is followed by `<`, attempts a backtracking type-id parse and takes it only if it
consumes cleanly to the closing paren; otherwise the position and the diagnostic count are restored
and the expression path runs as before. sizeof(expr) and sizeof(type) stay distinguishable.

Measured (a clean probe — the triage repro is malformed for clang): direct 64, viaAlias 64,
scalar 8, calls 1 on both backends. Suite 1085/0.

